# env files
.env
.env*.local
# ...and any copy of one. `.env*.local` anchors on the name ending in `.local`,
# so `.env.local.bak-preSSO` — a backup holding DATABASE_URL and
# AUTH_JWT_SECRET — was not ignored and would have been committed to a public
# repository by any `git add -A`. Backups are made under time pressure, which
# is exactly when nobody reads the staged file list.
.env*
!.env.example

